# Normalize every text file to LF in both the repository and the working tree.
#
# Why: this repo had no .gitattributes, so line endings and the UTF-8 BOM were
# decided by whatever tool wrote the file last. A README rewrite under
# core.autocrlf=true added a BOM and produced mojibake (UTF-8 read as
# Windows-1252). Pinning the encoding contract here makes the result
# deterministic instead of tool-dependent.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content and leave it untouched, so image
# and font assets stay safe.
* text=auto eol=lf
